    "New_PyDay01Audio04.mp3": {
      "src": "Day01/New_PyDay01Audio04.mp3",
      "duration": 83.9,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Here is the Master Data Types Reference matrix for data analysts.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.66
        },
        {
          "text": "The table is organised by category, exactly as it appears on screen.",
          "start": 4.32,
          "end": 8.46
        },
        {
          "text": "Starting with Numeric types: Integer, written int, is an arbitrary-precision whole number that never overflows.",
          "start": 9.18,
          "end": 15.96
        },
        {
          "text": "Float is an IEEE-754 double-precision decimal, ideal for currency and averages.",
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 23.2
        },
        {
          "text": "Complex stores real and imaginary parts for scientific work.",
          "start": 23.88,
          "end": 27.52
        },
        {
          "text": "Moving to Text: String, written str, is an immutable Unicode sequence and the workhorse for categorical columns.",
          "start": 27.52,
          "end": 35.26
        },
        {
          "text": "Boolean, written bool, is simply True or False, and it controls every analytical branch you write.",
          "start": 36.14,
          "end": 42.3
        },
        {
          "text": "The Sequence family holds ordered collections: List is mutable and perfect for a column of rows, Tuple is immutable and protects fixed records, and Range generates lazy integer sequences for memory-efficient iteration.",
          "start": 42.74,
          "end": 56.5
        },
        {
          "text": "Mapping means Dictionary, written dict, which stores key-value pairs and gives you lightning-fast O of 1 lookups using a hash table.",
          "start": 57.08,
          "end": 65.36
        },
        {
          "text": "Set types eliminate duplicates automatically and power fast union and intersection operations; Frozen Set is the immutable, hashable version safe to use as a dictionary key.",
          "start": 65.9,
          "end": 77.18
        },
        {
          "text": "And finally, NoneType is the singleton that represents missing or null data, just like SQL NULL.",
          "start": 77.6,
          "end": 83.6
        }
      ],
